/-! # The semisimple group generated by integral Chevalley exponentials

Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Section 23h, equation (153), Theorem 23.72
and Corollary 23.73, printed pp.510--511
(blueprint: lem-sfb-chevalley-root-exponential-group).

A finite integer basis identifies the scalar extension of the lattice with the
coordinate vector space used by the existing general linear group scheme.
The torus is the actual Hopf spectrum D(P), and its characters are normalized by e^lambda.
The normalizer reflection formula pins the coroots to the group-root convention;
character weights, rather than their differentials, are used in every characteristic.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.MonoidalCategory CategoryTheory.CartesianMonoidalCategory
open scoped CategoryTheory.MonObj

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

open Classical in
/-- Integral divided root exponentials generate the split semisimple group with
weight lattice P, the prescribed roots, and the prescribed integral coroots.

Source: Milne, Section 23h, equation (153), Theorem 23.72 and Corollary 23.73,
printed pp.510--511 (blueprint: lem-sfb-chevalley-root-exponential-group).

Proof plan:
1. Restrict the rational divided powers to the lattice and take their integer matrices.
   Nilpotence gives finite support. The identity D_i D_j = binom(i+j,i) D_(i+j)
   on the torsion-free lattice proves the additive group law integrally. Its inverse
   is the value at -a. The bracket with the Cartan shifts weights by m alpha, giving
   conjugation by the actual weight character, without dividing by a factorial in F.
2. Enumerate the roots, form f(a) as the ordered product of exponentials, and apply
   lem-sfb-affine-pointed-map-generated-subgroup to f(a)f(b)^(-1). Its image is
   inverse-stable and contains every generator. Affine space is geometrically reduced
   and connected. Apply lem-sfb-geometrically-reduced-group-smooth for smoothness.
3. Use lem-sfb-multiplicative-character-antiduality and Z Omega = P to embed D(P)
   by its weight action. Apply lem-sfb-diagonalizable-group-geometric-criteria for
   splitness. The simple coroots are a basis of the coroot lattice by
   lem-sfb-root-base-rational-integral-spans, so their cocharacters generate D(P).
   By lem-sfb-chevalley-integral-rank-one each lies in the generated subgroup,
   using diag(s,s^(-1)) = w(s)w(-1) in SL2.
4. Apply lem-sfb-chevalley-exponential-big-cell. The zero tangent-character space
   is exactly Lie(T), and the other characters are precisely R. By
   lem-ag-smooth-lie-local-dimension and lem-ag-group-identity-local-dimension,
   any larger torus has at most this dimension. Tori are smooth connected by
   lem-sfb-multiplicative-type-largest-subtorus; strict dimension growth from
   lem-sfb-solvable-normal-subgroup-products proves maximality.
5. The rank-one groups from lem-sfb-chevalley-integral-rank-one have root groups
   equal to the exponential images, by lem-sfb-reductive-root-subgroup-parametrizations.
   Their simple opposite-root commutations and Weyl conjugations give all hypotheses
   of lem-sfb-rank-one-reductive-generation. They generate H, hence H is reductive.
6. The same rank-one compatibility identifies each group coroot with c_alpha.
   Its pairing on a weight is precisely c_alpha(lambda), and its Weyl representative
   conjugates T by the stated reflection. The roots span P tensor Q; apply
   lem-sfb-semisimple-roots-span to get semisimplicity in the solvable-normal sense.
   If V = 0 and R is empty, P = 0, the generators are absent and H = T = 1.
No identification of the characteristic-p Lie algebra with an integral Lie form is claimed. -/
theorem chevalley_root_exponential_group
    (V : Type u) [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℚ V] [FiniteDimensional ℚ V]
    (R : Set V) (c : R → Module.Dual ℚ V)
    (_hfinite : R.Finite) (_hne : ∀ a : R, (a : V) ≠ 0)
    (_hspan : Submodule.span ℚ R = ⊤)
    (_htwo : ∀ a : R, c a a = 2)
    (_hint : ∀ a b : R, ∃ n : ℤ, c a b = (n : ℚ))
    (_hreflect : ∀ a : R, Set.BijOn (fun v : V ↦ v - c a v • (a : V)) R R)
    (_hreduced : ∀ a : R,
      R ∩ (Submodule.span ℚ ({(a : V)} : Set V) : Set V) = {(a : V), -(a : V)})
    (P : Submodule ℤ V)
    (_hP : ∀ v : V, v ∈ P ↔ ∀ a : R, ∃ n : ℤ, c a v = (n : ℚ))
    (g : Type u) [LieRing g] [LieAlgebra ℚ g] [FiniteDimensional ℚ g]
    (_hss : LieAlgebra.HasTrivialRadical ℚ g)
    (H : LieSubalgebra ℚ g) (_hab : IsLieAbelian H)
    (_hmax : ∀ K : LieSubalgebra ℚ g, H ≤ K → IsLieAbelian K → K = H)
    (θ : H ≃ₗ[ℚ] Module.Dual ℚ V) (e : R → g)
    (_he : ∀ a : R, e a ≠ 0 ∧ ∀ h : H, ⁅(h : g), e a⁆ = θ h a • e a)
    (_hdecomp : DirectSum.IsInternal (Sum.elim (fun _ : Unit ↦ H.toSubmodule)
      (fun a : R ↦ Submodule.span ℚ ({e a} : Set g))))
    (_hbasis : ∃ (r : ℕ) (b : Module.Basis (Fin r) ℚ V) (hb : ∀ i, b i ∈ R),
      (∀ a : R, (∀ i, ∃ n : ℤ, b.repr a i = (n : ℚ)) ∧
        ((∀ i, 0 ≤ b.repr a i) ∨ (∀ i, b.repr a i ≤ 0))) ∧
      ∃ B : Module.Basis (Fin r ⊕ R) ℚ g,
        (∀ i, B (Sum.inl i) = (θ.symm (c ⟨b i, hb i⟩) : g)) ∧
        (∀ a : R, B (Sum.inr a) = e a))
    (_hopp : ∀ a b : R, (b : V) = -(a : V) → ⁅e a, e b⁆ = (θ.symm (c a) : g))
    (_hstring : ∀ a b k : R, (a : V) + (b : V) = (k : V) →
      ∃ p : ℕ, (b : V) - p • (a : V) ∈ R ∧
        (∀ n : ℕ, (b : V) - n • (a : V) ∈ R → n ≤ p) ∧
        ∃ ε : ℤ, (ε = 1 ∨ ε = -1) ∧
          ⁅e a, e b⁆ = ((ε : ℚ) * (p + 1 : ℚ)) • e k)
    (_hzero : ∀ a b : R, (a : V) + (b : V) ≠ 0 → (a : V) + (b : V) ∉ R →
      ⁅e a, e b⁆ = 0)
    (W : Type u) [AddCommGroup W] [Module ℚ W]
    [LieRingModule g W] [LieModule ℚ g W] [FiniteDimensional ℚ W]
    (_hfaith : LieModule.IsFaithful ℚ g W)
    (Λ : Submodule ℤ W) (Ω : Finset V)
    (_hlattice : Submodule.IsLattice ℚ Λ) (_hfree : Module.Free ℤ Λ)
    (_hΩ : ∀ wt ∈ Ω, wt ∈ P ∧ LieModule.weightSpace W (fun h : H ↦ θ h wt) ≠ ⊥)
    (_hweights : DirectSum.IsInternal (fun wt : Ω ↦
      (LieModule.weightSpace W (fun h : H ↦ θ h wt)).toSubmodule))
    (_hgenerate : Submodule.span ℤ (Ω : Set V) = P)
    (_hintegral : DirectSum.IsInternal (fun wt : Ω ↦
      ((LieModule.weightSpace W (fun h : H ↦ θ h wt)).toSubmodule.restrictScalars
        ℤ).comap Λ.subtype))
    (_hnil : ∀ a : R, IsNilpotent (LieModule.toEnd ℚ g W (e a)))
    (_hdiv : ∀ (a : R) (m : ℕ) (w : W), w ∈ Λ →
      ((Nat.factorial m : ℚ)⁻¹ • (LieModule.toEnd ℚ g W (e a)) ^ m) w ∈ Λ)
    (F : Type u) [Field F] [IsAlgClosed F] :
    ∃ (I : Type u) (_ : Fintype I) (_ : DecidableEq I) (b : Module.Basis I ℤ Λ)
      (D : R → ℕ → Matrix I I ℤ) (N : R → ℕ),
      (∀ (a : R) (m : ℕ) (j : I),
        ∑ i : I, (D a m i j : ℚ) • ((b i : Λ) : W) =
          ((Nat.factorial m : ℚ)⁻¹ • (LieModule.toEnd ℚ g W (e a)) ^ m)
            ((b j : Λ) : W)) ∧
      (∀ (a : R) (m : ℕ), N a ≤ m → D a m = 0) ∧
      ∃ x : R → (Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.additive F) ⟶
          Grp.mk (GeneralLinearGroup I F)),
        (∀ (a : R) (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [Algebra F A] (z : A),
          (GeneralLinearGroup.homMulEquiv I F A
            (TorusCharacterTangent.additiveParameterPoint F z ≫ (x a).hom.hom)).val =
              ∑ m ∈ Finset.range (N a), z ^ m • (D a m).map (Int.castRingHom A)) ∧
        ∃ (G : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F)))) (iG : G ⟶ Grp.mk (GeneralLinearGroup I F))
          (y : R → (Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.additive F) ⟶ G)),
          IsClosedSubgroupScheme iG.hom.hom ∧ (∀ a : R, y a ≫ iG = x a) ∧
          (∀ (K : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F)))) (iK : K ⟶ Grp.mk (GeneralLinearGroup I F)),
            IsClosedSubgroupScheme iK.hom.hom →
            (∀ a : R, ∃ z : Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.additive F) ⟶ K,
              z ≫ iK = x a) → ∃ j : G ⟶ K, j ≫ iK = iG) ∧
          IsSemisimpleGroupScheme G.X ∧
          ∃ (iT : diagonalizableGroup F P ⟶ G)
            (_ : IsCommMonObj (diagonalizableGroup F P).X)
            (_ : IsCommMonObj (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F))
            (χ : P ≃+ Additive (diagonalizableGroup F P ⟶
              Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)))
            (ν : Module.Dual ℤ P ≃+ Additive
              (Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F) ⟶ diagonalizableGroup F P))
            (Q : RootDatum R P (Module.Dual ℤ P))
            (act : ModObj (diagonalizableGroup F P).X G.X)
            (s : R → (diagonalizableGroup F P ≅ diagonalizableGroup F P)),
            ReductiveTorusCentralizer.IsMaximalTorus iT ∧
            (∃ r : ℕ, Nonempty (diagonalizableGroup F P ≅ MultiplicativeType.splitTorus F r)) ∧
            (∀ lam : P,
              (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of (AddMonoidAlgebra F P))).hom
                ((χ lam).toMul.hom.hom.left.appTop
                  ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of (LaurentPolynomial F))).inv
                    (LaurentPolynomial.T 1))) = AddMonoidAlgebra.single lam 1) ∧
            (∀ (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [Algebra F A]
              (t : StandardGroupSchemes.affine F A ⟶ (diagonalizableGroup F P).X)
              (wt : Ω) (hwt : (wt : V) ∈ P) (w : Λ),
              (w : W) ∈ LieModule.weightSpace W (fun h : H ↦ θ h wt) →
              ∀ j : I,
                ∑ k : I, (GeneralLinearGroup.homMulEquiv I F A
                  (t ≫ iT.hom.hom ≫ iG.hom.hom)).val j k * (b.repr w k : A) =
                    TorusCharacterTangent.multiplicativePointCoordinate F
                      (t ≫ (χ ⟨wt, hwt⟩).toMul.hom.hom) * (b.repr w j : A)) ∧
            Module.Finite ℤ P ∧ Module.Finite ℤ (Module.Dual ℤ P) ∧
            Q.IsReduced ∧ (∀ a : R, (Q.root a : V) = (a : V)) ∧
            (∀ (a : R) (lam : P), (Q.coroot a lam : ℚ) = c a lam) ∧
            (∀ (lam : P) (f : Module.Dual ℤ P), Q.toLinearMap lam f = f lam) ∧
            (∀ (lam : P) (f : Module.Dual ℤ P),
              (ν f).toMul.hom.hom ≫ (χ lam).toMul.hom.hom =
                (𝟙 (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)) ^ (f lam)) ∧
            act.smul = (iT.hom.hom ⊗ₘ 𝟙 G.X) ≫ GrpObj.conj G.X ∧
            (∀ lam : P, (lam ≠ 0 ∧
              @TorusCharacterTangent.weightSpace F _ (diagonalizableGroup F P) G act
                (χ lam).toMul ≠ ⊥) ↔ lam ∈ Set.range Q.root) ∧
            (∀ (a : R) (lam : P),
              (s a).hom.hom.hom ≫ (χ lam).toMul.hom.hom =
                (χ lam).toMul.hom.hom /
                  (χ (Q.root a)).toMul.hom.hom ^ (Q.coroot a lam)) ∧
            (∀ a : R, ∃ a' : R, (a' : V) = -(a : V) ∧
              ∀ (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [Algebra F A]
                (t : StandardGroupSchemes.affine F A ⟶ (diagonalizableGroup F P).X),
                (t ≫ (s a).hom.hom.hom ≫ iT.hom.hom) =
                  (TorusCharacterTangent.additiveParameterPoint F (1 : A) ≫ (y a).hom.hom) *
                  (TorusCharacterTangent.additiveParameterPoint F (-1 : A) ≫ (y a').hom.hom) *
                  (TorusCharacterTangent.additiveParameterPoint F (1 : A) ≫ (y a).hom.hom) *
                  (t ≫ iT.hom.hom) *
                  ((TorusCharacterTangent.additiveParameterPoint F (1 : A) ≫ (y a).hom.hom) *
                  (TorusCharacterTangent.additiveParameterPoint F (-1 : A) ≫ (y a').hom.hom) *
                  (TorusCharacterTangent.additiveParameterPoint F (1 : A) ≫ (y a).hom.hom))⁻¹) ∧
            (Subsingleton V → R = ∅ →
              Nonempty (G ≅ Grp.trivial _) ∧
              Nonempty (diagonalizableGroup F P ≅ Grp.trivial _)) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
